cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or reference this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Equilibrium: A Reproducible Research Instrument for Bayesian Portfolio Construction under the Black-Litterman Framework"
abstract: >-
  Equilibrium implements the Black-Litterman pipeline end to end: reverse optimisation of
  CAPM-implied equilibrium returns, Bayesian posterior inference with explicitly calibrated
  view uncertainty, constrained mean-variance optimisation, walk-forward evaluation free of
  look-ahead in estimation, and historical and hypothetical stress testing. Returns are typed
  by economic kind (excess or total) and epistemic status (observation or estimate); the
  posterior is cross-validated across two algebraically equivalent formulations; and
  correctness is established against a hand-derived analytical example, closed-form limiting
  cases and independent re-implementations.
authors:
